    },
    {
      "id": "b-185",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. The YC Application Narrative"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-186",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Here's how you position this:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-187",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**One-Liner**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-188",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "> \"Agent-native operating system for personal data—giving AI persistent memory of your work.\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-189",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-190",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**What do you make?**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-191",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "> \"Nodebook unifies email, calendar, notes, and tasks into a computable graph that AI agents can reason about. Instead of 'goldfish memory' chatbots, agents have full context across your entire workflow. We're using LD-C (a spec we created for verifiable computation) as the foundation, ensuring agents can't hallucinate facts about your data.\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-192",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-193",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Why now?**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-194",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "> \"Apple Intelligence, Microsoft Copilot, and others are all moving toward 'agent-native computing,' but they're bolting agents onto existing apps. We're building the OS layer that makes this architecture work—persistent, queryable context that agents can act on. The shift is happening NOW.\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-195",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-196",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Traction**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-197",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "> \"We've been dogfooding for 3 weeks—I run my entire workflow through it. We have 10 alpha users, 3 of whom use it daily. The VS Code extension we built for LD-C tables (the foundation) has 500 installs in 2 weeks.\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-198",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-199",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Market**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-200",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "> \"Every knowledge worker is the market—but we're starting with solo operators (founders, researchers, executives) who already hack together Notion + ChatGPT + email. They're desperate for this. Later: expand to teams, then enterprise.\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-201",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-202",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-203",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
